  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mapping and mobilizing Jordanians abroad for skills and development in Jordan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x200b;&#x200b;This project aims to contribute to strategic, evidence-based policies that maximize Jordanian expatriates&#x2019; contributions to national development, while leveraging opportunities for skills mobility partnerships for Jordanians &#x200b;To achieve this objective, the project will support the Government of Jordan and key stakeholders to engage in the mobilization of Jordanian expatriates for skills mobility partnerships and other contributions to development in Jordan (Outcome 1), through the following outputs: - &#x200b;A gender-sensitive mapping report on Jordanian expatriate presence and possible contributions to national socioeconomic development is made available to key stakeholders (Output 1.1). - &#x200b;The Jordanian Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Expatriates, diplomats and other Government stakeholders have increased capacity to engage with expatriates and promote their participation in national development initiatives in a strategic and gender-sensitive manner (Output 1.2). - &#x200b;Women and youth in Jordan have increased access to gender-sensitive educational and labour opportunities based on consultations and initiatives with key public and private sector stakeholders (Output 1.3).&#x200b;</narrative>
  </description>
